    <string name="al_safety">How your data is protected</string>
    <string name="al_safe_1">Only reads the apps ticked above — everything else is ignored</string>
    <string name="al_safe_2">Alerts containing TAC / OTP codes are dropped, never stored</string>
    <string name="al_safe_3">Keeps only amount, shop and time — never the full text; card numbers keep the last 4 digits</string>
    <string name="al_safe_4">Never reads this app’s own reminders, so a bill reminder can’t be logged as a payment</string>
    <string name="al_safe_5">Everything is processed on the phone — the app has no internet permission</string>
    <string name="al_consent_title">Allow Lazee to read payment alerts?</string>
    <string name="al_consent_body">Lazee will read notifications only from the payment apps you tick, take the amount, shop name and time, and save those on this phone. It skips OTP / TAC messages, never keeps the full text, and never uploads anything — the app has no internet permission.\n\nNext, Android will open “Notification access”. Turn on Lazee there, then come back.</string>
